<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of verse in a single column of italic lines, stanzas separated by blank lines; catchword "Bases" at the lower right, below the last line.</layout>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>O, Rex tremende Cælitum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>O, cerne, &amp;t huius inferi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Fathiscat orbis machina</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Tanto malorum pondere</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Oppressa. Cerne &amp;t ingemens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Iam liberari flagitet.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Vix portiunculam tuus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Christus patentis obtinet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Mundi, licet nutu suo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Hæc cuncta Rex creauerit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Supremus, omnia &amp;̄ regat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Creata mente prouida.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Per tot procellas &amp;̄ truces</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Motus furentum protege</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Sacros potentior greges.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Lupique Romani impiam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Iustas ad iras concitus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Vindex Tyrannidem preme.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Timete gentes improba,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Horrete summum Iudicem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Deus, Deus &amp;iuentium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Furoris æstu flammeo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Vos insequutus proteret,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Vestrumque puniet scelus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Hunc ante grandis machina</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Liquetur orbis totius,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Et quotquot illam sustinent</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword "Bases" is set at the right, below the last line, and is given in bottom_margin as well as the text ends with the last full line. Ornamental and stain marks on the scan are omitted. Some letters in the long-s and ligature forms (e.g. "&amp;t", "&amp;̄", "&amp;iuentium") are uncertain and may be misread; "&amp;iuentium" is probably "&amp;iuentium" for "Iuuentium" with [?] not marked.</notes>
</page>
